# What the elder says when you pass by and they think well of you (US-162). A greeting is a short script: @bark names it, and the first
# line that holds is shown for a few seconds over their head. It is chosen like a conversation: their own name first, then a role, then the kind.
@who elder
@when opinion(npc, hero) >= 0
@priority 10
@bark greet

=== start
Elder: The fire keeps you well, {hero}.
